From: Open-Wine-Components <fixes@proton-ge-custom>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] gamefixes-steam: Add CPU topology clamp for Where Winds Meet (3564740, 3804320)

Where Winds Meet spawns worker threads matching logical CPU count.
On SMT-enabled high-core CPUs, spawning 13+ concurrent worker threads
oversaturates physical cores and causes high involuntary preemptions.
Clamping CPU topology to physical cores (no SMT) reduces workers to 6.
---
 gamefixes-steam/3564740.py | 12 ++++++++++++
 gamefixes-steam/3804320.py | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gamefixes-steam/3564740.py
 create mode 100644 gamefixes-steam/3804320.py

diff --git a/gamefixes-steam/3564740.py b/gamefixes-steam/3564740.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c78ba04
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gamefixes-steam/3564740.py
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+"""Game fix for Where Winds Meet"""
+
+from protonfixes import util
+
+
+def main() -> None:
+    """Where Winds Meet / Messiah Engine creates worker threads matching logical CPU count.
+    On multi-threaded CPUs (e.g. 8c/16t Ryzen 9800X3D), spawning 13+ concurrent worker threads
+    oversaturates physical cores and causes high involuntary preemption and long loading stalls.
+    Clamping CPU topology to physical cores (no SMT) reduces workers to 6 and matches P10-34.
+    """
+    util.set_cpu_topology_nosmt(core_limit=8)
diff --git a/gamefixes-steam/3804320.py b/gamefixes-steam/3804320.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ef71412
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gamefixes-steam/3804320.py
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+"""Game fix for Where Winds Meet Playtest"""
